{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310739,"nonce":"CbeJDlUsRyHutEIp/Qd4vreXTy0=","title":"2026-09-20 67384b1b+684a6078 (591-\u003e593): imported generic abstracts specialize from receiver type args; transitive callees bind their own ...","message":"**Monomorphization batch (67384b1b, issue e552e09):** calls on an imported\ngeneric abstract (`Vector\u003cInt\u003e.join`) and abstract ctors carried NO type args\ninto the MIR call (`call/direct.rs`, `call/mod.rs` FUNCTION_MAP path, and the\nctor HIR Call only read `TypeKind::Class`). `propagate_transitive_fixups` gave a\ngeneric callee the CALLER's substitution map zipped positionally onto the\ncallee's own params (`StringBuf.add\u003cT\u003e` got T=I32 → appended the string pointer\nas an int). Now the callee's own map comes from `extract_generic_call` on the\ncall instruction. `trace([0,7])` printed `[null,7]` — the untyped array\nformatter reads a zero slot as null; `array_to_string_fn(elem)` picks the typed\n`haxe_array_to_string_{i64,bool,f64}`. `RAYZOR_DUMP_MIR_MONO=1` dumps post-mono.\n\n**T→Dynamic (684a6078, issue b61401c):** `maybe_box_value_inner` SKIPPED\n`TypeKind::TypeParameter`, so `dyn():Dynamic return v` returned raw i64 bits;\n`box_value_for_dynamic` (Type.typeof path) boxed every T as Int. Both now use\n`box_type_param_for_dynamic` = `haxe_box_typed_ptr(bits, tag)` with a\n`type_param_tag_fixups` placeholder the monomorphizer fills (the mechanism the\nOptional-inner-T path already had). Runtime Reference arm tags a class instance\nfrom its header; Array/anon T still box untyped (MIR type arg is `Ptr(Void)`\nfor both — cannot be told apart at compile time); enum T (I64) boxes as Int.\n\n**Std.isOfType was globally broken:** `Std.isOfType(v, Int)` desugars to\nTypeCheck with `expected` = type of the `Int` EXPRESSION = StdTypes\n`abstract Int` (Float/Bool likewise; `String` = the String CLASS).\n`runtime_type_id` had no Abstract arm → 0 → every Dynamic check false, and\nevery static `Std.isOfType(7, String)` fell to the permissive `true`.\n`canonical_type_ref` (type_ids.rs) maps those four names to the primitive\nkinds. Haxe: an Int IS a Float (`haxe_std_is` + static arm).\n\n1. A `T` the current MIR function does NOT declare (`Type.createInstance`'s T\n   leaking into a non-generic caller, Issue8717) has nothing to fill its tag →\n   keep the old path (raw / `true`). Check `builder.current_function().signature.type_params`.\n2. A `T` ARGUMENT into a GENERIC callee's Dynamic formal stays RAW: an\n   unannotated param of a generic fn decays to Dynamic while the body reads it\n   as T (`ArraySort.upper(..., val)`, `TreeNode.new(l, k, v, r)`). Boxing put a\n   box in the key slot → `Reflect.compare` read it as the key →\n   test_balancedtree_crossmodule_mono SIGSEGV fault=0x5. **\"Dynamic\" in a\n   callee signature is often a DECAY, not a declaration.** The\n   unannotated-param inference now also reads bare `field = param` stores\n   (was `this.field = param` only) — `RAYZOR_PARAM_INFER_LOG=1`.\n\nIssue6722 (ArraySort.sort via a function-typed FIELD: unsorted / SIGSEGV /\nhang — issue 543e595) and Issue1827 (static inline `call(d1,d2)` untyped\nparams over `g++` args: different garbage each run then exit 139). A MOVED\nWRONG_ANSWER→CRASH on these is noise — run the row 3-5 times before chasing.\n\nProbes: scratchpad/probe/G2a (T→Dynamic shapes), G3d/G4a (isOfType vs `haxe --run`).\nFixture: haxe-conformance/regressions/TypeParamToDynamic.hx.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_type_param_to_dynamic_and_isoftype_type_ids` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}